# Elixir Koans - 07 Keyword Lists

```elixir
import ExUnit.Assertions
```

## Like maps, keyword lists are key-value pairs

```elixir
kw_list = [foo: "bar"]
```

```elixir
assert kw_list[:foo] == ___
```

## Keys may be repeated, but only the first is accessed

```elixir
kw_list = [foo: "bar", foo: "baz"]
```

```elixir
assert kw_list[:foo] == ___
```

## You could access the values of repeating key

```elixir
kw_list = [foo: "bar", foo1: "bar1", foo: "baz"]
```

```elixir
assert Keyword.get_values(kw_list, :foo) == [___, ___]
```

## Keyword lists are just special syntax for lists of two-element tuples

```elixir
assert [foo: "bar"] == [{___, ___}]
```

## But unlike maps, the keys in keyword lists must be atoms

```elixir
not_kw_list = [{"foo", "bar"}]
```

```elixir
assert_raise ArgumentError, fn -> not_kw_list[___] end
```

